<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- preview-devserver-reaper (cc-fleet-health, greenlit orch-console #72892/#72894/#72900,
       2026-10-21). Two disk CRITs the same day traced to the same root cause: an ad-hoc
       `next dev`/`vite` preview server left running after nobody was watching it, silently
       ballooning its own .next/dist build cache for hours. Detection gate: zero ESTABLISHED
       connections on the server's listening port for an idle-grace window (default 20min);
       for a REGISTERED fleet_lanes worktree with a LIVE tmux session, the lane's own pane
       must ALSO be idle (hard requirement) before reaping — never yanks a dev server a lane
       is driving programmatically. Orphans (no fleet_lanes row / no live session) reap on
       zero-connections-past-grace alone.
       STAGED ARMING (CLAUDE.md §2): DETECT-ONLY on first landing — this is fresh code, not
       yet wet-proven as an unattended automated loop (its detection logic WAS manually
       wet-proven live against real fleet data on 2026-10-21: both CRIT#1 op32368 and
       CRIT#2 cosem-exams-lane kills were done by hand using this exact signature before the
       tool existed). Arm with --apply only after a few ticks of sane detect-only output. -->
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>dev.wingmen.preview-devserver-reaper</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <string>cd "$HOME/wingmen/orchestrator" &amp;&amp; set -a &amp;&amp; . ./.env &amp;&amp; set +a &amp;&amp; unset ANTHROPIC_API_KEY &amp;&amp; exec .venv/bin/python3 -m scripts.preview_devserver_reaper --json</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>1800</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/logs/preview_devserver_reaper.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/logs/preview_devserver_reaper.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
